Subject: [PATCH] wasix: release signal wakers with their blocking futures

Backport Wasmer PR #7057 at 9d586e08e502002abda7996db6bb73b22030a63e:
https://github.com/wasmerio/wasmer/pull/7057

Each signal-waiting future owns a keyed registration, updates its current
waker and removes only its own registration on completion or cancellation.
Keep registration and pending-signal checks under the same mutex, preserve
live registrations across signals and retain anonymous one-shot subscriptions.
Additionally snapshot signal wakers under the mutex and invoke them after
unlocking, so a waker may re-enter the registry without deadlocking.

Adapt the syscall integration to this pinned runtime family, preserving its
existing guest-signal interruption and pending-link operation behavior.

Regression coverage checks retention, independent waits, waker replacement,
pending signals, thread changes, re-entry and actual blocking guest syscalls.
Remove this backport only when the selected upstream release supplies these
invariants and its product consumers pass the same regressions.

